# Commits that changed formatting only, and no behaviour. `git blame` skips
# them so it still reaches the person and the reasoning behind each line.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE IS NOT AUTOMATIC. Turn it on once, per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# (GitHub honours it without any configuration.)
#
# ⚠ AND ONLY PUT PURE REFORMATS HERE. The whole value of this file is that
# every hash in it is guaranteed to contain no logic — one behavioural change
# smuggled into a listed commit and blame silently lies about that line for
# ever. If a commit did both, it does not belong here; split it instead.
#
# The comments in this codebase are its best feature, and a 194-file whitespace
# commit would put a wall between every one of them and its reasoning. That is
# what this file exists to prevent.

